                    "text": "Here's the bug report content.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe roll is exited by the clip's animation event, and that event handles a **semantically different** thing than the input that starts the roll.\n\n- `Player_GroundedState.OnRollingStarted` (`D:/UnityProject/APRGSDemo/Assets/GM_Game/Scripts/Gameplay/Character/Player/StateMachines/Movement/States/GroundState/Player_GroundedState.cs:127`) fires on `Dash.started` and immediately switches to `RollingState`.\n- `Player_RollingState.Enter` (`.../Player_RollingState.cs:19`) calls `SetAnimationInputWeight(PlayableType.Movement, 4, 1)`.\n- `AnimaClipsData.SetMovementTarget` **resets every movement clip's time to 0** (that's why all states call it). So the `TriggerOnMovementStateAnimationTransitionEvent` event baked into `Roll.anim` at **`time: 0.4667`** (`D:/UnityProject/APRGSDemo/Assets/GM_Game/Animas/Player/Clip/Movement/Roll.anim:663798`) fires again on the very next clip evaluation → `Player_RollingState.OnAnimationTransitionEvent` (`.../Player_RollingState.cs:24`) runs immediately → `MovementInput == zero` → `LightStoppingState` (or `RunningState`).\n\nSo:\n\n- **1 press** = enter roll → same-frame transition event → exits to stopping/running. Looks like \"the roll ended instantly\".\n- **2 presses** = the second press arrives after the first roll already exited back into a state that still binds `Dash` (`Idle`/`Running`/`LightStopping` all derive from `Player_GroundedState`), so the roll restarts — and this time the transition event is consumed by the character having moved / the input no longer being zero, so the roll plays through.\n\nHence \"now it rolls on the second press\".\n\n## Fix\n\nThe event that ends the roll is currently indistinguishable from the stale event left over from entering the state. Add an event gate so a roll only accepts its transition once the clip has actually been evaluated from its start, and ignore the stale event. Also re-clamp `MovementInput` so the roll cannot end while input is still held in a transient state.\n\n```csharp:D:/UnityProject/APRGSDemo/Assets/GM_Game/Scripts/Gameplay/Character/Player/StateMachines/Movement/States/GroundState/Player_RollingState.cs\nusing UnityEngine;\nusing UnityEngine.InputSystem;\n\npublic class Player_RollingState : Player_GroundedState\n{\n    private Player_RollingData rollingData;\n\n    // 翻滚刚进入时动画时间会被重置，Roll.anim 里 0.4667s 的过渡通知会立刻被打出，\n    // 所以进入后的第一帧要丢弃这次通知，否则翻滚会瞬间结束\n    private bool bCanAcceptTransitionEvent;\n\n    public Player_RollingState(Player_MovementStateMachine playerMovementStateMachine) : base(playerMovementStateMachine)\n    {\n        rollingData = MovementData.RollingData;\n    }\n\n    public override void Enter()\n    {\n        base.Enter();\n\n        bCanAcceptTransitionEvent = false;\n\n        SetAnimationInputWeight(PlayableType.Movement, 4, 1);\n        stateMachine.ReusableData.MovementSpeedModifier = rollingData.SpeedModifier; //直接设置速度修正\n        AddForceOnTransitionFromStationaryState();\n    }\n\n    public override void Update()\n    {\n        base.Update();\n\n        //动画被重置后至少经过一帧，之后再来的过渡通知才是本段翻滚自己的\n        bCanAcceptTransitionEvent = true;\n    }\n\n    public override void OnAnimationTransitionEvent()\n    {\n        if (!bCanAcceptTransitionEvent) return; //丢弃进入翻滚瞬间的残留通知，修复\"要按两次才能翻滚\"\n\n        base.OnAnimationTransitionEvent();\n\n        if (stateMachine.ReusableData.MovementInput == Vector2.zero)\n        {\n            stateMachine.ChangeState(stateMachine.LightStoppingState);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        stateMachine.ChangeState(stateMachine.RunningState);\n    }\n\n    private void AddForceOnTransitionFromStationaryState()\n    {\n        if (stateMachine.ReusableData.MovementInput != Vector2.zero) return;\n\n        Vector3 CharacterRotationDirection = stateMachine.playerRef.transform.forward; //获取玩家向前方向\n\n        CharacterRotationDirection.y = 0;\n\n        stateMachine.playerRef.RigidBody.velocity = CharacterRotationDirection * GetSpeedMovement();\n    }\n\n    protected override void OnMovementCanceled(InputAction.CallbackContext context)\n    {\n\n    }\n\n    protected override void OnRollingStarted(InputAction.CallbackContext context)\n    {\n\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Why this is the right fix, not a workaround\n\n- It removes the **stale event** problem at its source instead of special-casing input counts. The roll now always accepts exactly the *first* legitimate transition event and always ignores the leftover one.\n- It is state-local: no change to `AnimaClipsData`, `StateMachine`, or the anim clip, so `Idle`/`Running`/`Stop` behavior is untouched.\n- `MovementInput` is also a useful secondary guard if you later add rolling while moving: the leftover event evaluates `MovementInput` from the *previous* frame's read, so gating on `bCanAcceptTransitionEvent` is what actually fixes the instant exit.\n\n## Verify (in Unity)\n\n1. Enter Play, stand still, press Space **once** → roll should play through and end in the stop animation, not cut out.\n2. Hold a direction + press Space → roll plays, ends in `RunningState`.\n3. Press Space twice quickly → the second press should be ignored during the roll (that's the intended no-op in `OnRollingStarted`), then a new roll should be possible after exiting.\n4. Check the Console: you should see exactly one `State Player_RollingState` per press.\n\n## Optional follow-ups (not required for this bug)\n\nTwo related issues you may want to address separately:\n\n1. **The Roll clip's exit event at 0.4667s is very early** for a ~4.0s clip (`Roll.anim:663798`, `m_StopTime`/sample rate give a 4.0167s clip). The roll currently always exits at ~0.47s; if the animation is supposed to be full-body, the event time (or the clip length) needs re-timing in the Animation window.\n2. **`Dash` isn't disabled during the roll's actual duration.** `PlayerInput.DisableActionInput(action, seconds)` exists (`.../Utilles/Input/PlayerInput.cs`) but is unused — a real cooldown/i-frame gate would be cleaner than relying on the no-op override.\n\nIf you want, I can also add the buffered/cooldown version of the dodge rather than the event-gate fix."
